entry.summary:
I spent an afternoon chasing SubmissionError / FiberFailure wrapping: RpcError 1010: Invalid Transaction: Custom error: 117
and a WASM panic that looks like feesWithMargin / transaction_merge Unreachable. The circuit compiled. The proof server was up. The genesis wallet had tDUST. The bug was in how I used Compact Map. This post is the lesson: on Midnight Local Undeployed, do not update an existing Map key. Insert a new key. If a value must become public, disclose() it. And hashing a witness then checking != empty is not access control. I verified this against a real local stack, not a sketch.
